 0030   0006    '----- UGLSCRL.BAS: does this card's display actually SCROLL / 
                page-flip?
 0030   0006    '----- Sets the same VESA 640x480x256 two-page mode the game us
                es, fills video
 0030   0006    '----- memory with 32-pixel colour bands (a rainbow on page 0, 
                shifted colours on
 0030   0006    '----- page 1) plus a white "ruler" bar on each band whose LENG
                TH = that band's
 0030   0006    '----- video-memory line / 2, so the bar at the very top of the
                 screen tells you
 0030   0006    '----- which memory line is being shown. Then it steps through 
                phases, each held a
 0030   0006    '----- few seconds after N beeps, changing ONLY how the display
                 start is set:
 0030   0006    '-----   P1  VESA 4F07h  -> line 0    (baseline: top band = RED
                , ruler bar tiny)
 0030   0006    '-----   P2  VESA 4F07h  -> line 32   (works? top band = GREEN)
 0030   0006    '-----   P3  VESA 4F07h  -> line 96   (works? top band = YELLOW
                )
 0030   0006    '-----   P4  uglSetVisPage 1          (page flip works? whole s
                creen shifts colours)
 0030   0006    '-----   P5  CRTC 0Ch/0Dh = 8192      (dword-unit card? top = G
                REEN, line 32)
 0030   0006    '-----   P6  CRTC 0Ch/0Dh = 32768     (byte-unit card? top = GR
                EEN, line 32)
 0030   0006    '----- If P2/P3 change the top colour, VESA scrolling works. If
                 only P5 or P6 do,
 0030   0006    '----- the card scrolls via the CRTC (we can use that). If noth
                ing but P1 ever
 0030   0006    '----- shows, the display cannot be moved on this card. Writes 
                UGLSCRL.LOG (the
 0030   0006    '----- 4F07h read-backs are logged too). Press any key to stop;
                 loops until then.
 0030   0006    DEFINT A-Z
 0030   0006    '$INCLUDE: 'UGL.BI'
 0030   0006    ''
 0030   0006    '' ugl.bi -- UGL routines
 0030   0006    ''
 0030   0006    
 0030   0006    Const UGL.TRUE%     = -1%
 0030   0006    Const UGL.FALSE%    = 0%
 0030   0006    
 0030   0006    Const DCTSIZE%      = 64%
 0030   0006    '' dc types:
 0030   0006    Const UGL.MEM%      = 0% * DCTSIZE%
 0030   0006    Const UGL.BNK%      = 1% * DCTSIZE%
 0030   0006    Const UGL.EMS%      = 2% * DCTSIZE%
 0030   0006    
 0030   0006    Const FMTSIZE%      = 128%
 0030   0006    '' color formats:
 0030   0006    Const UGL.8BIT%     = 0% * FMTSIZE%
 0030   0006    Const UGL.15BIT%    = 1% * FMTSIZE%
 0030   0006    Const UGL.16BIT%    = 2% * FMTSIZE%
 0030   0006    Const UGL.32BIT%    = 3% * FMTSIZE%
                                                                      PAGE   2
                                                                      13 Sep 26
                                                                      16:54:41
Offset  Data    Source Line      Microsoft (R) QuickBASIC Compiler Version 4.50

 0030   0006    
